WEBVTT

00:07:27.569 --> 00:07:31.257
MH: And it's very easy to fall into
a very hierarchical form of communication.

00:07:31.281 --> 00:07:34.311
AG: You know, where the person
with the most authority or status

00:07:34.335 --> 00:07:35.579
hijacks the conversation.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.186
In a classic study of airline crews,

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:41.828
it was possible to predict
a flight's timeliness and fuel efficiency

00:07:41.852 --> 00:07:43.806
just by watching the first 15 minutes

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.036
of a captain's meeting with the crew.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:49.776
The ineffective captains
tended to monopolize the conversation.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.776
The effective ones did
more two-way communication.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.805
They spent more time engaging their crews

00:07:54.829 --> 00:07:56.016
and listening to them.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.836
They also encouraged their crews
to talk to one another about the task.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.789
Creating open channels of communication